  "notes": [
    "SOURCE: pi05/out/menagerie/ufactory_xarm7/xarm7.xml (the WITH-gripper model). hand.xml is the same subtree standalone.",
    "IMPORTANT TRAP (identical to the arm links): MuJoCo's compiler recentres each mesh onto its inertial frame and stores the recovery in geom_pos/geom_quat, which compile to EXACTLY mesh_pos/mesh_quat (verified: |geom_pos-mesh_pos| = 0 and |geom_quat-mesh_quat| = 0 for all 7 gripper meshes). The raw STL attached at the BODY pose with an IDENTITY local transform is correct. Applying compiled geom_pos/geom_quat double-transforms and shifts parts by 5-37 mm.",
    "Verified numerically at a random arm pose with theta=0.37: two-sided Hausdorff distance between (body xpos/xquat) x raw-STL and MuJoCo's own (geom_xpos/geom_xmat) x compiled mesh_vert is 2.71e-09 m worst case over the whole gripper subtree, i.e. float32 STL rounding.",
    "Quaternions are xyzw (three.js). MuJoCo's native order is wxyz.",
    "xarm_gripper_base_link is COINCIDENT with link7's origin (body pos 0 0 0) and rotated 180 deg about link7's z (MJCF quat wxyz 0 0 0 1 -> xyzw 0 0 1 0). The gripper base is flush on the end of link7; the offset is exactly zero.",
    "THE LINKAGE IS AN EXACT PARALLELOGRAM. outer-knuckle pivot -> finger pivot = (0, 0.035465, 0.042039) and inner-knuckle pivot -> connect anchor = the same vector, so all six gripper joints take the SAME scalar theta and each finger TRANSLATES without rotating relative to the gripper base. Verified: the two `connect` equality residuals are 2.9e-17 m and the finger-vs-base relative rotation is 4e-06 deg at every theta in [0, 0.85].",
    "Each joint's `axis` already carries the correct sign, so you drive every moving body with the same +theta. Pivot is the body origin (jnt_pos = 0 0 0) for all six.",
    "theta = 0 is FULLY OPEN, theta = 0.85 rad is FULLY CLOSED. This is the opposite sense to our data channel, hence the (1 - g) in the mapping below.",
    "The MuJoCo actuator confirms the extremes: tendon `split` has coef 0.5 on each driver joint so its length IS theta, and the affine actuator settles at length = 0.333*ctrl/100, i.e. ctrl 0 -> theta 0 and ctrl 255 -> theta 0.84915.",
    "The real xArm gripper counts (0..850, 0 = closed) are the reverse of MuJoCo's ctrl (0..255, 0 = open). Do not carry the MuJoCo ctrl sense into the renderer.",
    "For rendering, use only these 7 mesh parts. The 4 `pad_box` geoms under `pads` are collision-only (MJCF group 3) and sit exactly flush with the finger meshes' inner faces; include them only for debugging.",
    "three.js is Y-up, this model is Z-up. Handle that once on the ROOT group, exactly as the arm links already do -- never per part."
  ],
